# .github/.releaseignore -- dev-only paths for the release gate (gitignore syntax).
# A merged PR whose changed files ALL match here releases nothing, unless it carries a
# semver:* label (an explicit label always wins). Anything not matched is product and
# releases as a patch. Read by .github/workflows/release.yml.
# NOTE git semantics: a file can't be re-included if a parent DIRECTORY is excluded.
#   docs/**  +  !docs/user/**   does NOT work (docs/user/ itself is excluded);
#   docs/**  +  !docs/user/  +  !docs/user/**   does. File-level `!docs/openapi.yaml` works.
#
# earmark specifics: the Dockerfile does `COPY . .` and .dockerignore drops docs/ and *.md
# except docs/openapi.go + docs/openapi.yaml (embedded in the binary), so only the markdown
# docs are dev-only. .dockerignore itself shapes the build context, so it is product.
# README*, runner/ (deployed ASR worker), deploy/helm/ (published chart) are product.

# CI, editor and agent config
/.github/
/.devcontainer/
/.claude/
/.vscode/
/.mcp.json
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
/CONTRIBUTING*

# Docs that are not embedded in the image (docs/openapi.{go,yaml} are product)
/docs/*.md
/docs/design/

# Tests
*_test.go
/runner/test_*.py

# Repo and linter config, local-only build files
/.gitignore
/.env.example
/.editorconfig
/.golangci*
/.pre-commit-config.yaml
/.markdownlint*
/.yamllint*
/Makefile
/compose.yaml
